---
import Slide from '../ui/Slide.astro';
import Callout from '../ui/Callout.astro';
import CodeBlock from '../ui/CodeBlock.astro';
import Pill from '../ui/Pill.astro';
---

<Slide
  id="s25b-layer-app-commands"
  chapter="Layers"
  title="Application & Business Logic — Commands"
  notes="Separate platform from app: exec curl localhost, logs, port-forward and inspect response body with jq. Myth: platform fine because pod Running — process started ≠ business logic works."
>
  <div class="stagger flex flex-col gap-6">
    <section>
      <h3 class="mb-3 font-display text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-deck-cyan">Typical commands</h3>
      <CodeBlock
        lang="bash"
        caption="Separate platform from app"
        code={`kubectl exec -it deploy/<app> -n <ns> -- curl -s localhost:8080/health
kubectl logs deploy/<app> -n <ns> --since=10m
kubectl port-forward svc/<app> 8080:80 -n <ns>
curl -s localhost:8080/api/orders | jq .   # inspect body, not just status`}
      />
    </section>

    <Callout type="myth">
      The platform is fine because the pod is Running. Running describes Pod lifecycle state — not application health.
    </Callout>

    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 border-t border-deck-border/60 pt-4">
      <Pill tone="amber">Decision hint</Pill>
      <span class="text-lg text-deck-muted">In-cluster curl + response body — if that fails, it is not "just Ingress."</span>
    </div>
  </div>
</Slide>
